From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Icefin Player <noreply@github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 03:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] vo_libmpv: gpu-next: start the colour adjustment from
 neutral

pl_video_render() filled five of struct pl_color_adjustment's six members and left `temperature` (the white point
shift) as whatever was on the stack, so an occasional frame was rendered at another white point: the same picture
with its colour shifted for one frame. Start from pl_color_adjustment_neutral, so that member and any libplacebo
adds later are neutral.

Reported by patrickjquinn on mpv PR #16818 (2026-09-16), with the one-line fix and before/after measurements.

Icefin Player.
---
diff --git a/video/out/gpu_next/video.c b/video/out/gpu_next/video.c
index 5c03093..a1ec67f 100644
--- a/video/out/gpu_next/video.c
+++ b/video/out/gpu_next/video.c
@@ -798,7 +798,7 @@ void pl_video_render(struct pl_video *p, struct vo_frame *frame, pl_tex target_t
     struct pl_render_params params = p->pars->params;
 
     // Declare a local struct to hold the color adjustment values.
-    struct pl_color_adjustment color_adj;
+    struct pl_color_adjustment color_adj = pl_color_adjustment_neutral;
 
     // Query the current brightness/contrast/etc values from the equalizer
     struct mp_csp_params cparams = MP_CSP_PARAMS_DEFAULTS;
